Shallow Copy: The copy in which changes applied to the nested/inner objects of copied item also reflects the original object structure but other than the nested/inner objects changes won't be applied.
This is known as Shallow copy.

import copy
original = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
shallow = copy.copy(original)
shallow[0].append(99) #Applying the changes to the nested/inner objects
print(shallow)
print(original)

#Applying the changes to the object other then nested list
shallow.append([5, 6]) 
print(shallow) 
print(original) 

Deep Copy: The copy in which changes applied to the nested/inner objects of copied item won't get reflects the original object structure.
This is known as Deep copy.

import copy
original = [[1, 2], [3, 4]]
deep = copy.deepcopy(original)
deep[0].append(88)    
print(original)
print(deep)     

